0,Wajarri - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wajarri,"July 23, 2025 - Boolardy Station, the site of the Murchison Radio-astronomy Observatory, lies on the traditional lands of the Wajarri people. The Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO) and the Australian Square Kilometre Array Pathfinder office have been working with the Wajarri ...",Wajarri,Australian
1,Wajarri language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wajarri_language,"Wajarri (/ ˈwɒdʒəri / WOJ-ə-ree, natively [wacari]) is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language. It is one of the Kartu languages of the Pama–Nyungan family.",Wajarri,Australian
2,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"1 week ago - The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and musical instrumentation that are unique to particular regions or Aboriginal Australian groups; and some elements of musical tradition are common or widespread through much of the Australian continent, and even beyond.",Wajarri,Australian
3,List of Indigenous Australian musicians - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Indigenous_Australian_musicians,"February 16, 2026 - This is a list of Indigenous Australian musicians.",Wajarri,Australian
4,Edie Maher - Wajarri - YouTubeWajarri language - WikipediaGodfrey Simpson -Wajarri - YouTubeWajarri - Wikipedia,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4RD70X39wj4,"Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube. Wajarri (/ ˈwɒdʒəri / WOJ-ə-ree, natively [wacari]) is an endangered Australian Aboriginal language. It is one of the Kartu languages of the Pama–Nyungan family. Feb 27, 2018 · Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube. The Wajarri people, also spelt Wadjari, Wadjarri, Watjarri, and other variations, are an Aboriginal Australian people whose traditional lands are in the Mid West region of Western Australia.",Wajarri,Australian
